{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg73Z5CzcNwjgepimEyEk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't confirm the latest stable Rust. The sources I found disagree, and both look stale.\n\n- **Third-party tracker:** Versionlog lists Rust 1.96.1 (30 Jun 2026) as the newest, after 1.96.0 on 28 May 2026.\n- **Official blog listing:** The snapshot I got stops at 1.94.1 (26 Mar) and 1.94.0 (5 Mar).\n\nToday is 2026-10-17, and Rust ships a new stable version every six weeks. By that schedule, 1.96.0 on 28 May would be followed by roughly 1.97 in early July, 1.98 in mid-August and 1.99 in late September or early October. So 1.96.1 is probably not the current release.\n\nTo get the real answer, run `rustup update stable && rustc --version`. You can also open [blog.rust-lang.org/releases/latest](https://blog.rust-lang.org/releases/latest), which redirects to the newest release post.\n\nSources:\n- [Rust Blog releases](https://blog.rust-lang.org/releases)\n- [Versionlog Rust](https://versionlog.com/rust/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1049,"cache_read_input_tokens":18575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1049},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68391403-3d97-4202-8dcf-1c4ea2ef30ef","uuid":"307c1dd1-c8d9-4f65-86f9-35eabe395007","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:46:59.437Z","request_id":"req_011Cg73Z4w8P38KCjHAbjpsL"}
